#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124225 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124659 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1bc2396-f949-57a0-be50-d5606abe3372" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Standard Form"}] :question/id #uuid "d2479726-b486-5bc2-864f-98a3659d81d5" :question/math-academy-id "e-1470" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)=x^2+4x+6?$" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny = ax^2+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=1>0,$ $b=4,$ and $c=6.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx= -\\dfrac{b}{2a} = -\\dfrac{4}{2 \\cdot 1} = -2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=-2$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}+4x+6 \\\\  & =(-2)^{2}+4(-2)+6 \\\\  & =4-8+6 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-2,2),$ and the range of the function is $[2,\\infty).$\n\n![](images/41/41b7219793120c0e37b3d910ef6a8f3754c1d9f27b784f937381743d7b7a85df.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124226 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124660 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb0d6e0e-bf61-5fe9-bf8a-ab15c5846e11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Factored Form"}] :question/id #uuid "f69335f5-b5df-5053-8127-a7489c711b5f" :question/math-academy-id "e-1472" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x) = -\\dfrac{1}{2}(x+3)(x-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny = a(x-x_1)(x-x_2),\n$$\n\nwith $a = -\\dfrac{1}{2} <    0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward. Consequently, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are $x_1=-3$ and $x_2=1,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{-3+1}{2}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=-1$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x+3)(x-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-1+3)(-1-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-1,2),$ and the range of the function is $(-\\infty,2].$\n\n![](images/2f/2f949680675dd0b0347adc154b8be6ce301ddb2f5b1b9ab0c077a5c00f81568f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124391 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124583 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "713fb1a0-5d7b-5cde-aafe-de5887086e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Domain of a Quadratic Function"}] :question/id #uuid "59873e3c-c8ba-5844-874a-01cf298b361d" :question/math-academy-id "e-7992" :question/problem "What is the domain of the function $g(x)=\\dfrac{4}{3}x^2+5x -12?$" :question/worked-solution "A quadratic function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the domain of $g(x)$ is $x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124393 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124584 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56d457de-8511-5870-98e3-b81e72e60585" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Vertex Form"}] :question/id #uuid "d6a69eb7-e598-51e8-92e9-fad42b3c0978" :question/math-academy-id "e-8027" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x) = (x+3)^2-2?$" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny = a(x-h)^2 + k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=-3$ and $k=-2,$ the vertex is $(-3,-2).$\n\n- Since $a=1>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, the vertex corresponds to the minimum output, while there is no maximum output. \n\nTherefore, the range is $[-2,\\infty).$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/57/579eef7814c2b51c44cded6fb2dc64e36d1106d359864e1e7ec7354511f80681.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124866 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124584 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56d457de-8511-5870-98e3-b81e72e60585" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Vertex Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf6aa7c8-bb56-5bf4-95c1-36f9ddf48788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[- \\frac{1}{2}, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121797} {:answer/id #uuid "fbf10690-55e7-5e23-9f0e-8e0943c19be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2}, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121798} {:answer/id #uuid "176e245e-9f72-51b8-b3cf-2258997a3486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- ∞, \\frac{5}{6}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121799} {:answer/id #uuid "67182b2e-e7f7-50af-b9f7-acbebdf1ce0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- ∞,-\\frac{1}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121800} {:answer/id #uuid "778d49d3-b3fa-55c8-b79f-9d8b41a3f398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[- \\frac{5}{6}, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121801}] :answer-field/id #uuid "600d4fe3-3e54-5f82-b63d-17a852bf35e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121796}] :question/id #uuid "1930d180-4cc3-5e28-910d-7be8bef132f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-34886" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x) = (x + \\frac{5}{6})^{2} - \\frac{1}{2}$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124584 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56d457de-8511-5870-98e3-b81e72e60585" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Vertex Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17490e92-f04a-51f7-b438-199eeb712801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549361} {:answer/id #uuid "8e98df84-9ac6-56f7-ab33-a824ee4007cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549593} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d59e6e-34b2-5e9c-b08e-8f2105c0bb6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549686} {:answer/id #uuid "ec8b8a2d-5b31-5cfd-aa2c-e0f8c2791516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549751} {:answer/id #uuid "f856d9c9-25b2-55b1-83a5-4041c1afdc91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec8b8a2d-5b31-5cfd-aa2c-e0f8c2791516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549751} :answer-field/id #uuid "d506de6d-4e6d-5568-a53f-79ffc50374e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0bc8d353-4f35-531e-9326-d4dcbc01bbdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-35908" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $y=f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-3?$" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=1$ and $k=-3,$ the vertex is $(1,-3).$\n\n- Since $a=1>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output. \n\nTherefore, the range is $[-3,\\infty ).$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/26/265532f4f4726151444ed873b875fc62c3c32a690a0ac859a318e2d4dc8fd285.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124583 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "713fb1a0-5d7b-5cde-aafe-de5887086e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Domain of a Quadratic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9b722a3-37a9-587e-9dea-9c2092f95778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [- 6, 6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122181} {:answer/id #uuid "0e4fd432-034a-5d15-9018-7e24f3316b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122182} {:answer/id #uuid "1460048c-f347-51ca-b111-02d73ac08676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ (- ∞, 6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122183} {:answer/id #uuid "4e5b7902-c19b-5525-b16f-7574db104d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [- 6, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122184} {:answer/id #uuid "7ce2c5b0-ecd9-5c69-ad26-eb999776aeb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x ∈ [6, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122185}] :answer-field/id #uuid "1a218775-00da-5a4d-bfc3-fc215fca31e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122180}] :question/id #uuid "0b78d132-27ad-5a99-9537-835ebfa56a00" :question/math-academy-id "q-35910" :question/problem "What is the domain of the function $f(x) = (x + 6)^{2} - 6$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 